data protection is a concern for many EU  citizens be it when using social  networks buying products online or  simply surfing the web most people want  to be sure that their personal data will  not be improperly used EU ministers of  Justice have been working on a proposal  to ensure high protection of personal  data across Member States during the  justice and Home Affairs Council in June  they intend to reach an approach to be  negotiated with the European Parliament  home affairs ministers in their turn  have migration issues at the top of  their agenda following the tragic events  in the Mediterranean in April EU leaders  agreed to mobilize all efforts to  prevent the death of more people at sea  and to address the root causes of  migration in May the European Commission  presented a communication defining  immediate measures to prevent human  tragedies by strengthening the EU  presence at sea and by targeting  criminals mulling networks fight against  terrorism is also on the agenda ensuring  the security of citizens preventing  radicalization and the cooperation with  international partners are the main  pillars of Europe's counterterrorism  efforts the council will evaluate the  progress in the implementation of  anti-terrorism measures
 

